requirements:
Establishes standard materials for all block components: 
a) Cheeks: Grey Cast Iron (IS 210 Gr 25), Spheroidal Graphite Iron (IS 1865 Gr SG 38), Whiteheart (IS 2107) or Blackheart (IS 2108) Malleable Iron, C20 wrought carbon steel (IS 1570), or Cast Steel (IS 1030);
b) Sheave: Siemens Martin wrought steel C20 or fully killed open-hearth steel C15 (IS 1570);
c) Axle Pin, Locking Plate, and Hinged Straps (Main & Locking Pieces): fully killed open-hearth steel C15;
d) Pin for Hinged supporting strap: wrought carbon steel C30;
e) Supporting Cross-Head: wrought steel C15 or Cast Steel (IS 1030);
f) Oval Eye, Head Fitting, and Round Nuts: wrought carbon steel C20.

Specifies detailed cheek dimensions (in mm) for nominal sizes 150 to 400. Examples:
a) Size 150: h1 = 150 mm, h2 = 50 mm, d2 = 25 mm, h3 = 166 mm, h4 = 71 mm, d3 = 35 mm, l5 = 55 mm, s1 = 3 mm, t5 = 26 mm, b2 = 50 mm, b3 = 24 mm;
b) Size 400: h1 = 400 mm, h2 = 130 mm, d2 = 70 mm, h3 = 445 mm, h4 = 189 mm, d3 = 90 mm, l5 = 145 mm, s1 = 7 mm, t5 = 78 mm, b2 = 130 mm, b3 = 62 mm.
